                <pb facs="0117" n="3" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg3"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">859b.01/9</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Danish Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Brun</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-29"><hi rendition="#italic">September 29,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 330</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With further reference to your note to me
                    of August 3d 1921 regarding Greenland, I beg to inform you as follows:</p>
                <p>The text of your said note was, as I had the honor to advise you by my letter of
                    August 8th,<anchor n="4" xml:id="d5-f1"/> submitted to the Danish Government by
                    me and in reply the Danish Minister of Foreign Affairs now instructs me to
                    inform you that the Danish Government has no desire to transfer its interests in
                    Greenland and has not given to any Government any right of preemption in
                    Greenland or any part thereof.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. Brun</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
